  :progress/schema-note "cloud-itonami-lei universe-expansion progress tracker, per ADR-2607199960. Distinct from the sibling ISIC/ISCO classification-sampling progress files: this file's company source is real, published stock-index constituent lists (one row per index), not an ISIC/ISCO top-N judgment call. Each :index/constituents entry that reaches :company/status :done gets the SAME cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI> repo treatment (real GLEIF LEI, real ToS fetch, provenance, no fabrication) as the ISIC/ISCO fleet -- and before creating any new repo, the LEI must be checked against ALL already-registered LEIs (this file + both sibling files) to avoid duplicate repos for a company that's already covered via an ISIC/ISCO row or another index. This file is the resume point for the next /loop iteration on the universe track (kept separate from the ISIC/ISCO resume points so the two tracks can proceed independently without stepping on each other)."
  :progress/resume-from "Iteration 2 done 2026-07-19 (same session day, separate /loop pass). sp500 is :index/status :in-progress with 14 constituents attempted total (9 :done, 5 :tos-fetch-failed) -- see that row's :index/constituents and :index/note. This iteration attempted 6 of the previously-listed untried candidates: Bank of America Corporation and Wells Fargo & Company were found to ALREADY have real GLEIF LEIs recorded elsewhere in this catalog (dedup hit against the pre-extracted registered-LEI list -- both were previously attempted under another row with :tos-fetch-failed outcomes; not re-attempted here, not re-listed in this row to avoid a duplicate entry) -- so the 6 genuinely new attempts were Goldman Sachs Group Inc. (done, as \"The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc.\"), Pfizer Inc. (done), Merck & Co. Inc. (done, as \"Merck & Co., Inc.\"), Adobe Inc. (tos-fetch-failed), Mastercard Incorporated (tos-fetch-failed), Caterpillar Inc. (tos-fetch-failed). Companies NOT yet attempted for sp500 (real, well-known S&P 500 constituents; Bank of America and Wells Fargo removed from this list since they are already registered elsewhere in the catalog under a different LEI-dedup row): Citigroup Inc., Morgan Stanley, Berkshire Hathaway Inc., Chubb Limited, MetLife Inc., Eli Lilly and Company, AbbVie Inc., Salesforce Inc., Honeywell International Inc., Deere & Company, Colgate-Palmolive Company, Kimberly-Clark Corporation, Mondelez International Inc., Netflix Inc., Meta Platforms Inc., Apple Inc., Alphabet Inc. -- resume by GLEIF-verifying and ToS-fetching more of these (dedup against the LEIs already in this row + both sibling progress files first) until sp500 reaches a documented stopping point, then mark :index/status :done and move to nikkei225 (next in file order), followed by topix100, ftse100, dax40, stoxx600, hangseng, csi300, asx200, tsx60, sensex, kospi200, bovespa, cac40, smi in that order. Same per-company discipline throughout: real GLEIF LEI only, real ToS fetch (WebFetch first; if it 403s/404s/times-out, retry once via homepage footer-link scan and/or a direct curl+plain-text-extraction fallback with a standard browser User-Agent before giving up), never fabricate, never substitute a subsidiary LEI for a parent, record failures honestly, dedup against this file + both sibling ISIC/ISCO progress files before creating any repo -- ALSO cross-check the live `gh api orgs/cloud-itonami/repos` listing since the pre-extracted registered-LEI snapshot can itself go stale between iterations (verified via direct curl to api.gleif.org/api/v1/lei-records/<LEI> this iteration, not just WebFetch summarization, after two GLEIF WebFetch summaries were found to omit the legalJurisdiction field). This superproject checkout has heavy concurrent multi-session activity -- always re-read this file fresh immediately before editing (this iteration hit a shallow-clone false-positive 'forced update'/'unrelated histories' on fetch, confirmed via `gh api .../compare` to be a pure 20-commit fast-forward, resolved with `git fetch --deepen=30` rather than treating it as a real force-push), and prefer a worktree outside the superproject + feature branch + `gh api .../merges` server-side merge over direct edits in the shared checkout. Separately this iteration, isco-1330 (Independent IT Services Management Practice) was topped up from 1 to 5 companies in the sibling isco-progress.edn file -- see that file's :progress/resume-from for its own next-step detail; not duplicated here."
