    :index/note "First seed pass, 2026-07-19: 8 candidates attempted, chosen to diversify away from the oil/pipeline/utility/airline/retail/chemicals/semiconductor/aerospace/waste sectors already heavily sampled by the ISIC track -- banking (JPMorgan Chase), CPG (Procter & Gamble, Coca-Cola), healthcare (Johnson & Johnson, UnitedHealth Group), payments (Visa), industrials (3M), and tech (Microsoft). 6/8 succeeded. JPMorgan Chase & Co. and Johnson & Johnson both had real GLEIF-verified LEIs but failed ToS fetch (bot-blocked/JS-shell) after 2 URL attempts each. All 6 successes used a curl+plain-text-extraction fallback after WebFetch alone 403'd/404'd/timed-out/summarized-instead-of-quoting on the same URLs for 5 of the 6 (only Visa needed just the redirect-follow). Iteration 2, same day: 6 more candidates attempted -- banking (Goldman Sachs), pharma (Pfizer, Merck), payments/tech (Mastercard, Adobe), industrials (Caterpillar). 3/6 succeeded (Goldman Sachs and Merck fetched directly via WebFetch on the first URL attempt with no retry needed; Pfizer needed the curl+footer-scan fallback after its first guessed URL 404'd). Adobe and Caterpillar were both fully bot-blocked at the network layer (Adobe: HTTP/2 stream reset + later HTTP 000 connection failure on both WebFetch and curl attempts against multiple hostnames; Caterpillar: HTTP 403 on every attempted hostname/path including the plain homepage) -- not just a wrong URL guess. Mastercard was HTTP 403 via both WebFetch and curl on its known terms-of-use path and its homepage; no substitute privacy-notice document was found on this pass (unlike Visa's precedent) so it was recorded as a clean tos-fetch-failed rather than stretched into a doc-type substitution. Bank of America Corporation (LEI 9DJT3UXIJIZJI4WXO774) and Wells Fargo & Company (LEI PBLD0EJDB5FWOLXP3B76) were both GLEIF-verified as real during this iteration's candidate research but turned out to already be recorded (with :tos-fetch-failed status) under a different progress-file row from earlier catalog work -- correctly not re-added here to avoid a duplicate LEI entry across files; see :progress/resume-from for detail."
